-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream work
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
model/motionbricks_mlx/ is a port to Apple MLX of MotionBricks
(https://github.com/NVlabs/motionbricks, v0.2.0, commit 54fc563):

    Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Files carrying the header "MLX port of MotionBricks" were translated from the
upstream PyTorch sources (tools/onnx/models/**) and modified: re-implemented in
MLX with a channels-last tensor layout, unified SOMA/G1 code paths, and added
compilation, reduced-precision and quantization options.

model-rs/ is a Rust port of model/motionbricks_mlx (files carrying the header "Rust
port of motionbricks_mlx"): an op-for-op port on mlx-rs, and a model-specific Metal
runtime with its own Metal kernels. Its GEMM kernel follows the tiling scheme of MLX's
steel GEMM (fragment layout, interleaved simdgroup tiles, serpentine accumulation);
MLX is MIT-licensed, Copyright © 2023 Apple Inc., and is not redistributed here.
model/motionbricks_mlx/assets/rig_kernels.metal holds Metal transcriptions of the
upstream rig geometry, shared by both ports.

tools/onnx/ ports upstream's ONNX exporter (tools/onnx/ at the same commit): it emits
the same batched FP32 and mixed-FP16 inference graphs from the verified checkpoints,
without PyTorch. tools/onnx/proto/onnx.proto3 is the ONNX message definition from the
onnx 1.23.2 release, Copyright ONNX Project Contributors, Apache License 2.0 -
licenses/onnx-Apache-2.0.txt.

model/motionbricks_mlx/runtime/ and model-rs/src/runtime/ port upstream's Runtime
API (motionbricks/model/, motionbricks/runtime/, motionbricks/animation/,
motionbricks/io/, motionbricks/utils/ at the same commit), with the same
Copyright and license. The Warp kernels were rewritten as NumPy and Rust code with
Warp's math conventions. TensorRT inference was replaced by the MLX model, the Metal
runtime or the mlx-rs port, and a BVH-based skeleton loader replaced the USD one.
model/examples/{_rig,generate_once,locomotion_loop}.py and model-rs/examples/
{support/runtime_rig,generate_once,locomotion_loop}.rs are ports of upstream
docs/examples/.

model/docs/runtime_api.md and model-rs/docs/runtime_api.md are adapted from
upstream docs/runtime_api.md, Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES,
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changes: rewritten for the MLX and
Rust ports, demo-runtime sections removed, setup, differences and verification
sections added. Each page carries this attribution.

MotionBricks paper: T. Wang et al., "MotionBricks: Scalable Real-Time Motions with
Modular Latent Generative Model and Smart Primitives", ACM TOG 45(4), 2026.

